2.3. Comparison of overset grid method and VBM for rotor model under analysis
Overset grid method requires a geometry, therefore, CATIA V5 is used for that purpose. Structured hexahedral mesh is generated in ICEM CFD. The details of geometric model are mentioned in the next section. The mesh generated on blades is made fine near the tips in order to capture vortices. The first wall distance was kept small enough to keep y+ values below 1. Value of thrust obtained in hover at 7000 r/min for isolated rotor model is 2.75 N using overset grid method. Similar analysis is carried out employing VBM. Grid independence study is carried out to get the suitable accuracy comparable with overset grid method and reasonable mesh size. Three meshes were prepared and their corresponding thrust values were compared with value obtained using overset method. The value obtained from overset grid method is kept as standard to compare results of different VBM meshes, since overset grid method is quite famous for its accuracy. A detailed comparison of the methods along with computational cost involved is shown in Table 1. Medium size mesh characteristics employing virtual blade method is selected for the further analysis of different octocopter configurations in hover and forward flight. A cylindrical region for each rotor disc with 0.015R disc density and two background grids on complete octocopter are utilized herein.
