4. Conclusions
(1) Results obtained using VBM method for current analysis matches with the experimental results showing the capability of VBM to predict rotor-to-rotor interaction with good accuracy and less computational cost. Therefore, VBM is a suitable selection for current study. (2) For coaxial configuration, loading effect is dominant with 0.125R vertical spacing which becomes insignificant with more spacing, where wake interaction phenomenon dominates with total thrust of the configuration fairly constant. The impact of rotor-to-rotor interaction increase for bigger diameter rotors with tip-to-tip interaction also coming into play which is not apparent in normal rotors. Conventional configuration rotors behave like isolated rotors in hover. (3) In forward flight, impact of rotor-to-rotor interaction is less than that in hover with upper rotor layer only interacting at 270°–360° azimuth of lower layer of coaxial rotor. Fore rotors wake also interact only with rear part of the aft rotors with lesser impact than coaxial rotor effect. The vortices from blades move with the flow
and merge to form larger vortex. Larger rotors bring tip-to-tip interaction on half of the azimuth of each rotor with interference angle depending on rotation direction and location of rotor. (4) In hover, coaxial configuration shows 11.89% and 14.22% loss in thrust compared to conventional and hybrid configurations with normal rotors and 15.61% loss compared to hybrid configuration with bigger diameter rotors. Coaxial square configuration performs worst in steady forward flight, with 9.1%, 14.77% and 18.8% loss in lift compared to coaxial diamond, conventional and hybrid configurations and with bigger diameter rotors, it shows loss of 17.82% and 9.96% lift compared to hybrid and coaxial diamond configurations. Loss in forward force is not very significant. The influence on torque magnitude shows slight deterioration for coaxial configurations in hover and forward flight. Combined figure of merit for each configuration in hover and forward flight confirms that hybrid configuration outperforms other configurations in overall aerodynamic performance.
